<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Playwright MCP</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 42rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; line-height: 1.5; }
    code, pre { background: #f4f4f5; padding: 0.15em 0.35em; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; }
    pre { padding: 1rem; overflow-x: auto; }
    .token { word-break: break-all; user-select: all; }
    h1 { font-size: 1.5rem; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Playwright MCP</h1>
  <p>Remote browser automation for MCP clients (ChatGPT agents, Cursor, etc.).</p>

  <h2>MCP endpoint</h2>
  <p><code id="mcp-url">${MCP_PUBLIC_URL}/mcp</code></p>

  <h2>API token</h2>
  <p class="token"><code id="api-token">${MCP_TOKEN}</code></p>
  <p><small>Persisted in app storage. Regenerate only by deleting <code>/app/data/api-token</code> via debug shell and restarting.</small></p>

  <h2>Example client config</h2>
  <pre id="client-config">{
  "mcpServers": {
    "playwright": {
      "url": "${MCP_PUBLIC_URL}/mcp",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer ${MCP_TOKEN}"
      }
    }
  }
}</pre>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>This endpoint can navigate the web and run scripts in a real browser. Use a strong token and restrict who can reach this app.</p>
</body>
</html>
